  "chapter": {
    "number": 56,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(57) For the end. Destroy not: by David, for a memorial, when he fled from the presence of Saul to the cave."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Have mercy, upon me, O God, have mercy upon me: for my soul has trusted in you: and in the shadow of your wings will I hope, until the iniquity have passed away.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will cry to God most high; the God who has benefited me. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He sent from heaven and saved me; he gave to reproach them that trampled on me: God has sent forth his mercy and his truth;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and he has delivered my soul from the midst of lions'whelps: I lay down to sleep, though troubled. As for the sons of men, their teeth are arms and missile weapons, and their tongue a sharp sword.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Be you exalted, O God, above the heavens; and your glory above all the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They have prepared snares for my feet, and have bowed down my soul: they have dug a pit before my face, and fallen into it themselves. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My heart, O God, is ready, my heart is ready: I will sing, yes will sing psalms.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Awake, my glory; awake, lute and harp: I will awake early.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, I will give thanks to you among the nations: I will sing to you among the Gentiles.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For your mercy has been magnified even to the heavens, and your truth to the clouds.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Be you exalted, O God, above the heavens; and your glory above all the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": []
  },
